---
/**
 * Who we are — personal, grounded, explains the name.
 * Not a bio. A statement of identity and philosophy.
 * SUCCESS: Stories (origin), Unexpected (the name), Emotional (personal).
 */
---

<section class="py-28 md:py-36 bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-6 lg:px-12">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-24">
      <!-- Left — the name and philosophy -->
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.25em] text-gray-400 uppercase mb-5 font-body"
        >
          Who we are
        </p>
        <h2
          class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-heading font-bold text-gray-950 leading-tight mb-8"
        >
          Kaizen.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-gray-950 leading-snug mb-6">
          It's a Japanese word. It means continuous improvement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-500 font-body leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Not "launch and leave." Not "build it and forget it." The idea that something can always be better — and that small, consistent changes beat big expensive overhauls every time.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-500 font-body leading-relaxed">
          We chose the name because it's how we actually work. Your website isn't a one-off project. It's a living thing that should get sharper every month.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right — the personal bit -->
      <div class="lg:pt-16">
        <div class="kaizen-about-block">
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 font-body leading-relaxed mb-6">
            We're based on the Wirral, working with businesses across the UK. Most of the people we help are small to mid-sized companies who know their website isn't doing its job — but don't know where to start fixing it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 font-body leading-relaxed mb-6">
            We're not a big agency with layers of account managers. When you work with Kaizen, you deal with the same person from first conversation to final delivery. No handoffs. No surprises. No "I'll pass that on."
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 font-body leading-relaxed">
            We'd rather do fewer projects properly than rush through dozens. If we take you on, you get full attention — not whatever's left after the bigger clients.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a
          href="/about/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 mt-10 font-heading font-bold text-lg text-gray-950 transition-all duration-200 hover:gap-5"
        >
          More about us
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="transition-transform duration-200"
          >
            <path d="M5 12h14" />
            <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .kaizen-about-block {
    border-left: 2px solid rgb(229 231 235);
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .kaizen-about-block {
      padding-left: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
